WEBVTT

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:05.060
Zero Arena's general manager will 
be coming to an IDOLiSH7 concert.

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:06.820
You dropped this.

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:14.280
Before the clock strikes 12, 
cast a spell on the audience!

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.620
Nanase-san, open your mouth!

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:19.370
No, we can't waste this chance!

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:23.370
Their center couldn't come 
onstage during the encore.

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:26.700
Do you know why, Tenn?

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:29.210
Yes. I know why, Kujo-san.

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:32.110
After all, we're twins.

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:35.460
Discover...

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:39.510
Let's go find it together (the future)

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:41.660
There's a glimmer I want 
to realize with you

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:47.730
Look, it's right here waiting 
for us (Let's jump!)

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:53.070
Wow...

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:03.330
As though we're weaving together 
our aspiration (Sing a song)

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:08.790
The melody paints a giant constellation

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:13.550
No matter what tomorrow's like,
 it won't betray us

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:19.260
We'll change even the harshest environments

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:21.850
(Some day!) A magnificent Dream

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:24.390
(Always!) The evening calm's Mild

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:29.900
Aim for distant lands! "Be with you!"

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:31.440
Discover...

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:35.240
A map of the stars (if we follow it)

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:40.870
We'll never look down Smile for you!

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:42.160
Night sky

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:46.120
Let's run across it together (to the future)

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:48.500
There's a glimmer I want 
to realize with you

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:54.170
Look, it's right here waiting 
for us (Let's jump!)

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:59.470
Wow...

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:11.980
That concert was seriously crazy!

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:20.600
<b>Riku</b>

00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:15.390
I know. I loved it so much!

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:18.010
I'm so excited for their regular show.

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:20.610
Me, too. I'm definitely going to record it.

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:26.290
By the way, I wonder why Riku-kun 
didn't come onstage at the end.

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:29.950
It seemed like he was pretty 
exhausted during the second half.

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:32.630
Maybe he wasn't feeling well.

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:34.630
<b>Nanase Riku</b>

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:39.130
I want him to do his best, but 
not so much that he collapses.

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:40.700
Yeah.

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:51.150
Riku-san, the car is ready.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:56.150
I... I'm sorry...

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:04.160
#03 The Proposal

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:08.680
How is Riku-kun doing?

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:12.880
We had him stay at the hospital overnight 
and return to the dorm this morning.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.380
He seems to have mostly recovered.

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:20.130
I see. Regardless of whether we're 
chosen for the inaugural show or not,

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:22.490
I hope he doesn't worry about it.

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:23.640
Me, too.

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:25.610
Good morning.

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:26.640
Morning.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:28.850
Good morn—What?!

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:32.100
Iori-san?! Yamato-san?!

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:33.980
What's going on?!

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:37.230
We're going to meet with 
Zero Arena's general manager

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:40.370
directly to give him a presentation 
on IDOLiSH7's past achievements.

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:41.490
What?

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:41.490
What?

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:45.410
Honestly, I'm not interested 
in the inaugural show.

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:48.720
But at this rate, Riku will 
never stop worrying about it.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:51.410
And for him, there's 
nothing worse than stress.

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:54.870
I'm not particularly concerned 
with Nanase-san's mental state,

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:57.370
but if we're to be judged solely 
based on yesterday's concert,

00:03:57.810 --> 00:03:58.920
that's a problem.

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:01.330
U-Um...

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:05.840
Zero Arena General Manager

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:08.880
I'm the general manager of Zero Arena.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:10.270
My name is Tanaka.

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:11.980
Welcome to our office!

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:17.740
Your concert yesterday was fantastic.

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:21.820
There are still some rough edges,

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:28.170
but your performance had the passion 
and unity of Zero's concerts.

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:31.500
Thank you.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:36.460
Zero Arena is the holy land 
of the legendary idol Zero.

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:39.680
We'd like to use its renovation 
as an opportunity to reinvigorate

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:42.010
the idol industry like it was 
when Zero was still around.

00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:45.260
TRIGGER will perform on the first 
day of the inaugural concert,

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:47.510
and Re:vale will perform on the last.

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:52.770
And we're thinking of having 
IDOLiSH7 perform on the second day.

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:55.730
You mean...

00:04:55.730 --> 00:05:01.900
Yes. We'd like you to appear 
in Zero Arena's inaugural show.

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:05.470
I have one concern.

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:09.120
What happened to your center?

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:16.710
He didn't appear in the encore 
during yesterday's concert.

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:21.710
Nanase is currently feeling 
under the weather.

00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:24.760
Is he sickly?

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:28.260
No, he was just exhausted yesterday.

00:05:28.630 --> 00:05:30.050
Normally there's no problem.

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:31.140
Ichi.

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:35.640
I'm sorry you had to see such 
a disgraceful performance.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:39.020
I guarantee we'll do better
 at the inaugural show.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:41.150
I'm relieved to hear that.

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:45.130
In that case, I hope you'll bring 
new energy to the holy land of idols

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:47.610
alongside Re:vale and TRIGGER.

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:49.070
We will.

00:05:57.390 --> 00:06:00.370
Ichi, why did you say that?

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:02.750
What are you talking about?

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:06.200
Don't play dumb. I'm talking about Riku.

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:09.010
You hid the fact that he's sickly.

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:14.340
Nanase-san has completed 
concerts until now.

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:16.390
He should be able to continue doing so.

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:18.140
You said once that

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:21.270
you're helping manage the group
 without the other members knowing.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:24.690
Please don't tell the others.

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:27.730
I don't intend to tell them,

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:31.950
but you should take Riku's feelings
 under more consideration.

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:35.120
Nanase-san's feelings?

00:06:35.470 --> 00:06:38.070
Riku is an honest and earnest guy.

00:06:38.070 --> 00:06:40.230
He gives everything his best effort.

00:06:40.730 --> 00:06:44.880
I get why you want to bet on 
him during critical moments.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:49.310
But don't put too much responsibility on him.

00:06:49.310 --> 00:06:50.510
It'll crush him.

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:55.640
I feel the opposite way.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:59.770
I felt guilty that we didn't 
allow Nanase-san to sing.

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:02.860
Did you want to make him sing 
until he collapsed onstage?

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:05.520
That's not what I meant!

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:11.410
Well, I suppose it means that 
Producer Izumi's expectations for Riku

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:13.530
are just that high.

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:19.790
Be careful.

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:23.210
You, Riku, and I are only human.

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:25.920
If you stick too rigidly to ideals and plans,

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:29.700
what was working before 
will eventually stop.

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:36.600
Seriously? Seriously? Seriously? Seriously?!

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:41.950
Y-Yeah. The general manager came to the 
office earlier to make a formal offer.

00:07:41.950 --> 00:07:43.600
Yes!

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:47.730
Let's stand on the same stage Zero 
did and make tons of people happy!

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:49.890
Okay, okay.

00:07:48.970 --> 00:07:51.970
Amazing! Wonderful!

00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:53.740
We did it, Nagicchi.

00:07:56.230 --> 00:07:57.240
Iori-kun.

00:07:57.240 --> 00:08:00.000
I was about to bring 
Riku-kun something to eat.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.620
Want to come with me?

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:02.430
What?

00:08:03.730 --> 00:08:05.730
He was worried about you.

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:09.830
He thought you must be angry that 
he didn't perform during the encore.

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:16.290
I'll pass. I have other things to do.

00:08:17.270 --> 00:08:17.890
I see.

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:19.890
I'll carry that.

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:22.190
Thanks.

00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:24.450
Tamaki-kun, you're so hardworking.

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:26.810
You did a great job cleaning 
the living room, too.

00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:30.320
It's 'cause my mom got sick and died.

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:33.850
Oh, right.

00:08:33.850 --> 00:08:35.640
Need anything else?

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:37.540
I'm fine, thanks.

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:38.200
Okay.

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:45.100
I'm glad IDOLiSH7 was chosen to 
perform at the inaugural concert.

00:08:46.690 --> 00:08:49.540
I'm glad I didn't hold everyone back.

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:53.770
I'm the most glad that 
you're feeling better!

00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:57.450
I'm pretty fine during the afternoon.

00:08:57.450 --> 00:08:59.820
It's worst at night and in the morning.

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:03.640
Sorry. Is my coughing too loud?

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:06.070
Don't worry about it.

00:09:06.070 --> 00:09:07.730
Is there anything you want us to do?

00:09:08.140 --> 00:09:11.650
Remember how you said 
Kujo-san and I are alike?

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:15.240
What would your brother do for you 
when you had an asthma attack?

00:09:15.710 --> 00:09:18.530
You're like him?

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:24.830
Does that mean he also tries to stab you
 with knives or throw computers at you?

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:26.870
Tamaki-kun, you're unbelievable.

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:29.000
I just got a little heated, is all.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:29.680
What?!

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:34.130
Just? A <i>little</i>? H-Heated?

00:09:35.980 --> 00:09:39.610
Tenn-nii would do anything for me.

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:42.830
Since our parents worked 
nights, when I was struggling,

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:45.330
it was Tenn-nii who'd be at my side.

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:49.430
When I had asthma attacks, 
I couldn't sleep lying down.

00:09:49.870 --> 00:09:52.870
I'd use his stomach as a pillow to sleep.

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:56.440
It would relieve my symptoms 
so I could sleep until morning.

00:09:57.060 --> 00:10:01.160
So I'm always reminded of that 
whenever I have an attack.

00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:02.790
I see.

00:10:04.930 --> 00:10:07.300
Riku-san, may I come in?

00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:09.170
Come in.

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:10.650
Excuse me.

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:12.930
Heya.

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:13.710
Good evening.

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:15.670
Good evening.

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:18.870
How are you feeling?

00:10:19.460 --> 00:10:23.720
I'm fine. I actually feel 
well enough to get up.

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:26.060
We should get going.

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:27.090
'Kay.

00:10:28.510 --> 00:10:31.400
Manager, you can be Rikkun's pillow.

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:32.150
Huh?!

00:10:33.310 --> 00:10:37.690
Your stomach seems like it 
would be softer than ours.

00:10:37.690 --> 00:10:38.150
Hey!

00:10:41.090 --> 00:10:42.980
Pillow? Stomach?

00:10:42.980 --> 00:10:46.900
N-No, no! Uh, um...

00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:49.410
I know. Let's turn on the TV.

00:10:49.910 --> 00:10:53.670
<i>You're such a vulnerable woman, 
entering my room like this.</i>

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:55.800
<i>Have you forgotten that I'm a man?</i>

00:10:56.730 --> 00:10:58.490
Are you all right, Riku-san?

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:00.800
I-I'm fine.

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:03.720
<i>A man and a woman alone 
in a room together.</i>

00:11:04.060 --> 00:11:06.470
<i>There's only one thing they could be doing.</i>

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:07.470
<i>Eek!</i>

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:09.820
<i>Maybe I'll confess my love.</i>

00:11:10.450 --> 00:11:12.060
<i>To you, of course.</i>

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:15.860
Let's not watch TV.

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:17.420
Um... okay.

00:11:17.420 --> 00:11:20.250
Dang it, Tamaki.

00:11:20.250 --> 00:11:21.910
Um, Riku-san.

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:23.350
Yes?

00:11:23.350 --> 00:11:25.290
Please answer me honestly.

00:11:25.770 --> 00:11:27.750
Is work hard for you?

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:28.580
What?

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:32.660
You're essential to IDOLiSH7.

00:11:33.090 --> 00:11:37.590
But I don't want to push you too hard.

00:11:39.610 --> 00:11:41.760
It's fine, Manager.

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:44.340
I should be apologizing for 
causing trouble for you.

00:11:44.650 --> 00:11:46.670
I'll do a better job managing my health.

00:11:46.670 --> 00:11:47.720
Riku-san...

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:49.220
I'll do my best.

00:11:49.550 --> 00:11:54.780
I promise I'll make our namesake show 
and the inaugural concert a success.

00:11:55.220 --> 00:11:56.990
Don't worry.

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:08.240
Is everything all right?

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:12.340
Ah, yes! It seems Riku-san 
is able to get up today.

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:15.290
No, Manager. I was asking about you.

00:12:18.780 --> 00:12:23.300
Sometimes I get a strange feeling 
while looking at Riku-san.

00:12:24.020 --> 00:12:28.960
I go back and forth between wanting to 
cheer him on from the bottom of my heart

00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:35.340
and asking him not to work so hard.

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:41.070
As his manager, I wonder 
what I should be feeling.

00:12:44.270 --> 00:12:46.750
Regarding MEZZO",

00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:50.700
if we add recording the namesake 
show on top of their existing work,

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:54.150
it may become even more difficult 
to manage the schedule.

00:12:54.570 --> 00:12:56.590
With magazine interviews, 
we should be able to...

00:12:57.770 --> 00:12:58.460
Manager?

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:01.660
Iori-san.

00:13:01.660 --> 00:13:02.460
Yes?

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:09.030
Let's change IDOLiSH7's center.

00:13:11.380 --> 00:13:13.230
Change the center?

00:13:13.940 --> 00:13:15.350
Are you insane?

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:18.460
Our schedule is going to become even tighter.

00:13:18.990 --> 00:13:22.730
There's promoting the namesake 
show, releasing new songs,

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:25.070
"Untitled" 
Program Plan

00:13:22.730 --> 00:13:25.070
and even more appearances on music programs.

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:28.240
After the concert, I spoke with the doctor.

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:32.340
As the weather changes, Riku-san's 
attacks will only get worse.

00:13:32.340 --> 00:13:33.840
Yes, but...

00:13:33.840 --> 00:13:36.300
It's just until Riku-san's 
condition stabilizes.

00:13:37.700 --> 00:13:41.160
The entire nation will be 
watching the namesake show.

00:13:41.160 --> 00:13:43.780
It's an important chance to be 
seen and increase our recognition

00:13:43.780 --> 00:13:46.510
among people who aren't 
interested in new idols.

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:49.860
Nanase-san must remain the center.

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:53.310
Even if they don't know the 
names of the other members,

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:55.600
they need to know the names 
IDOLiSH7 and Nanase Riku.

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:59.650
If we mess this up, Nanase Riku 
will never be our center again.

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:02.070
I promise we'll restore 
Riku-san to the center.

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:06.890
That's not what I'm talking about.

00:14:07.340 --> 00:14:09.850
First impressions are critical.

00:14:09.850 --> 00:14:12.830
Besides, who would you 
make the center instead?

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:16.080
I think you'd be a good choice.

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:18.500
Me?

00:14:19.410 --> 00:14:22.560
I think you're the best fit.

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:24.300
We'd be fresh, smart...

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:27.590
An IDOLiSH7 that can overcome any failures.

00:14:29.670 --> 00:14:32.150
You may not like it,

00:14:32.650 --> 00:14:36.180
but when I saw you get down on yourself 
after making a mistake onstage,

00:14:36.850 --> 00:14:39.350
it made me want to support you.

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:49.740
Maybe it's a strange thing to say, but 
I thought it was charming, like Riku-san.

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:57.020
Like you said, I might be the best fit 
if we were to choose another center.

00:14:57.460 --> 00:15:00.050
The personalities of the other 
members are too strong.

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:03.500
I would make for a plain IDOLiSH7.

00:15:03.990 --> 00:15:04.540
Then...

00:15:04.860 --> 00:15:06.930
That's another story, though.

00:15:06.930 --> 00:15:09.030
Nanase-san will sing for us.

00:15:09.030 --> 00:15:11.710
Nanase-san himself wants to sing.

00:15:11.710 --> 00:15:15.510
With his voice and character, we 
could reach Re:vale, or even Zero.

00:15:20.330 --> 00:15:22.590
Do you think I'm being stubborn?

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:28.630
Riku, are you feeling okay?

00:15:28.630 --> 00:15:30.320
Yeah, I'm fine!

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:32.160
Are you sleeping well?

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:35.950
Thanks. I heard you and 
Tamaki cleaned the dorm?

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:40.620
Yes. We worked together to make 
the it carpling spleen for you.

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:42.240
Sparkling clean.

00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:44.130
We made it sparkling clean.

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:48.800
Thanks. Iori, are you mad?

00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:50.110
Why do you ask?

00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:53.730
Because I couldn't sing
through the whole concert.

00:15:53.730 --> 00:15:56.510
I'll make sure it never happens again.

00:15:56.970 --> 00:15:58.500
I'm not mad.

00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:00.930
I'm just glad you're all right.

00:16:03.100 --> 00:16:06.690
I promise I'll become a superstar 
who pulls you guys along!

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:07.690
Just kidding.

00:16:09.330 --> 00:16:11.320
I expect great things from you.

00:16:14.220 --> 00:16:15.350
It's TRIGGER.

00:16:18.900 --> 00:16:22.040
Good morning. We look forward 
to working with you today.

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:24.140
It's good to see you again, Tsumugi.

00:16:25.770 --> 00:16:27.170
Did you change your hairstyle?

00:16:28.020 --> 00:16:29.750
Yes, a little.

00:16:29.750 --> 00:16:31.420
Unbelievable...

00:16:31.420 --> 00:16:33.670
It looks good on you. It's cute.

00:16:33.670 --> 00:16:35.220
Thank you.

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:39.460
The guy voted sexiest man alive 
is fully exhibiting his talents.

00:16:39.460 --> 00:16:41.180
Has her hairstyle changed?

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:43.560
I've been too busy to notice.

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:46.730
At this rate, we're just a bunch 
of good-for-nothings.

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:48.730
Okay, Nagi. Get in there!

00:16:47.660 --> 00:16:48.730
Oh! What?

00:16:48.730 --> 00:16:49.730
Sorry!

00:16:50.740 --> 00:16:51.970
Whoops.

00:16:52.930 --> 00:16:53.990
Are you okay?

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:55.100
There it is!

00:16:55.100 --> 00:16:58.050
The sexy beast with a lucky perv's timing!

00:16:58.050 --> 00:17:00.730
Where did you learn such obscene words?

00:17:00.730 --> 00:17:03.160
I saw it in a magazine headline.

00:17:03.670 --> 00:17:05.420
I'm sorry, Tsunashi-san.

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:09.490
It's fine. I'm glad we'll be
 working together today.

00:17:09.490 --> 00:17:12.430
I heard your namesake show is 
starting. I'm looking forward to it.

00:17:12.430 --> 00:17:13.560
Thank you.

00:17:13.560 --> 00:17:15.300
Can we stop this ridiculousness?

00:17:17.980 --> 00:17:19.890
Good morning.

00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:21.640
Tenn-nii.

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:24.890
Good morning. I haven't seen 
you since the <i>Black or White</i>.

00:17:25.210 --> 00:17:29.190
I'll tell you why I left home.

00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:32.140
Um, do you have time later?

00:17:32.140 --> 00:17:34.900
If not, could you at least give 
me your contact information?

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:35.970
Sure.

00:17:35.970 --> 00:17:37.010
Really?

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:39.490
But first, answer me this.

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:41.950
How do you feel about your 
blunder at your concert?

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:52.050
You couldn't participate in the encore.

00:17:52.050 --> 00:17:54.530
You gave your fans an 
incomplete performance.

00:17:54.530 --> 00:17:57.470
As a professional, you failed 
to complete your job.

00:17:57.470 --> 00:17:58.260
Am I wrong?

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:02.760
Tenn, that's too harsh.

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:04.550
You had your reasons, right?

00:18:04.550 --> 00:18:06.970
At least shut up and give him your number.

00:18:06.970 --> 00:18:07.840
He's your little brother—

00:18:07.840 --> 00:18:08.900
Stay out of this, outsiders.

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:10.900
<i>You're </i>the outsider here.

00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:19.910
Stop. Stop for a minute.

00:18:24.530 --> 00:18:27.540
Riku-kun, you don't seem 
well. Are you okay?

00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:29.780
We're still in rehearsal, 
so you can take a break.

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:33.190
No, I'm fine.

00:18:34.110 --> 00:18:35.990
Riku, take a break.

00:18:35.990 --> 00:18:38.220
We have the actual show after this.

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:39.410
I'm fi—

00:18:41.090 --> 00:18:43.810
What's wrong with him?
It seems like he's in pain.

00:18:45.640 --> 00:18:46.810
Hey, Tenn!

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:48.310
I'll do it.

00:18:50.740 --> 00:18:51.820
Kujo.

00:18:52.870 --> 00:18:54.900
Don't stop the rehearsal.

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:57.500
Do you think this is your personal studio?

00:18:58.010 --> 00:18:59.030
Tenn-nii...

00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:01.320
Move.

00:19:06.070 --> 00:19:07.330
Can you do the dance?

00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:09.130
Who do you think you're asking?

00:19:09.660 --> 00:19:12.180
Let's get started, please.

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:19.450
<i>Tenn-nii was mad.</i>

00:19:19.450 --> 00:19:21.770
<i>I've never seen him scowl like that.</i>

00:19:22.210 --> 00:19:24.590
<i>It's because I couldn't sing properly.</i>

00:19:24.590 --> 00:19:26.760
<i>Because I couldn't go onstage for the encore.</i>

00:19:28.690 --> 00:19:30.600
Let's resume rehearsal!

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:32.740
Three, two...

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:39.650
Yes, Dancing BEAT!! Even farther away

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:42.610
Night and day!! I want to deliver

00:19:42.610 --> 00:19:46.080
Never knowing what it means to stand still

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:53.370
Our future will be eternally Shooting!

00:19:56.580 --> 00:20:03.510
La la la la… forever wish

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:09.640
La la la la…

00:20:03.830 --> 00:20:05.390
<i>Wow.</i>

00:20:11.890 --> 00:20:18.400
La la la la…

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:27.950
Okay, good.

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:32.830
Thank you.

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:38.170
You were a huge help. Thank you so much.

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:39.960
Thank you, Kujo-san.

00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:42.340
Rehearsal isn't just a dry run.

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:46.340
Increasing excitement in 
the studio in preparation

00:20:46.340 --> 00:20:48.300
for the actual performance is our job.

00:20:48.300 --> 00:20:52.810
The staff and fans will always 
respond to our sincerity.

00:20:53.430 --> 00:20:57.150
Don't use your poor health as an 
excuse for your irresponsibility.

00:20:58.610 --> 00:21:01.110
Kujo-san, you're not wrong.

00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:03.370
I'd like to ask you one thing, though.

00:21:03.370 --> 00:21:04.030
Hey, Ichi!

00:21:06.820 --> 00:21:10.660
Would you have done the same 
thing to another group?

00:21:12.070 --> 00:21:12.660
What?

00:21:12.660 --> 00:21:14.530
You wouldn't have.

00:21:14.530 --> 00:21:19.290
It's because we're IDOLiSH7.
Because your unworthy brother is here.

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:20.560
Iori-san.

00:21:20.560 --> 00:21:22.580
You're like a helicopter parent.

00:21:22.580 --> 00:21:25.510
And because of that,
he grew up into a spoiled baby

00:21:25.510 --> 00:21:27.550
who can't do anything on his own!

00:21:28.780 --> 00:21:30.050
What?

00:21:30.710 --> 00:21:32.310
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

00:21:30.710 --> 00:21:32.310
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:36.050
You can't say that, Ichi. 
They're the ones who helped us.

00:21:36.050 --> 00:21:37.310
I'm really sorry.

00:21:37.310 --> 00:21:41.890
Tenn, Iori-kun's right. You shouldn't 
interfere so much with another agency.

00:21:41.890 --> 00:21:43.320
I'm really sorry.

00:21:43.320 --> 00:21:46.090
It's fine. Let's go for 
some of these sometime.

00:21:46.090 --> 00:21:47.680
Yes, let's!

00:21:47.680 --> 00:21:49.240
Come on, Tenn. Come here.

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:52.170
What? Did you click your tongue?

00:21:52.170 --> 00:21:53.410
Hey, you!

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:55.080
Ichi, calm down!

00:21:59.110 --> 00:22:03.380
Riku, it's fine. You finished the actual show.

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:05.210
I'm sorry.

00:22:05.630 --> 00:22:08.310
I keep causing trouble for everyone.

00:22:08.740 --> 00:22:10.860
I keep holding the group back.

00:22:10.860 --> 00:22:11.970
Riku-kun.

00:22:20.590 --> 00:22:21.530
Yes?

00:22:23.980 --> 00:22:25.250
Iori-san.

00:22:25.790 --> 00:22:26.990
Manager.

00:22:28.060 --> 00:22:30.930
I admit it. You were right.

00:22:28.660 --> 00:22:33.940
<i>(If you get lost, there's a song here)</i>

00:22:31.570 --> 00:22:33.460
I was wrong.

00:22:33.460 --> 00:22:34.300
What?

00:22:34.990 --> 00:22:38.490
I accept your proposal to change centers.

00:22:34.990 --> 00:22:40.000
<i>(If you get lost, there's a song here)</i>

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:45.710
We came to understand a brilliant something

00:22:46.390 --> 00:22:51.930
resembling all the light in the galaxy

00:22:52.550 --> 00:23:04.320
Even on days I'm scared, the faint 
warmth I want to deliver won't disappear

00:23:04.320 --> 00:23:10.530
Even if you want to close your 
eyes to reality's reflection

00:23:10.530 --> 00:23:16.180
Come on, let's create an illusion

00:23:16.180 --> 00:23:18.620
The sound of the future

00:23:19.620 --> 00:23:22.840
On the curtain of three thousand worlds

00:23:22.840 --> 00:23:26.090
We quietly adorn

00:23:26.090 --> 00:23:31.260
Each and every one of us has meaning

00:23:31.840 --> 00:23:35.220
It's the message of the Fantasia

00:23:35.220 --> 00:23:39.740
You're the one who gave 
me the courage to weave

00:23:39.740 --> 00:23:44.980
So I always want you by my side

00:23:55.640 --> 00:24:00.250
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:55.640 --> 00:24:00.250
<b>"A New Form"</b>
